course: dictionary
lesson: 9948
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Tartar is a good example. «A brown crust on a pet's teeth is tartar» is about teeth, so here it is a hard coating that builds up when teeth are not cleaned well.
explain: Read the words around it. In «tartar sauce», the word sauce tells you it is food. In «cream of tartar», the word baking tells you it is a powder. The clues are often in the next few words.
explain: Ask: what meaning would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check that it still makes sense. If it does not, try another meaning or look it up.
fact: Tartar is a hard yellowish coating that builds up on teeth if they are not cleaned well.
fact: Plaque left for days can harden into tartar, and only a dentist or hygienist can scrape it off.
fact: Tartar sauce, also called tartare, is a creamy sauce with pickles, often eaten with fish.
fact: Cream of tartar is a white powder used in baking.
fact: A Tartar, more correctly Tatar, is a member of a Turkic people of Russia and Central Asia.
exercise: «A brown crust on a pet's teeth is tartar.» What is tartar in this sentence? | A white powder used in baking | *A hard coating that builds up on teeth | A creamy sauce eaten with fish
exercise: Mum says, «Pass the tartar with the fish and chips.» Which meaning fits best? | A fierce, bad-tempered person | A hard coating on teeth | A member of a Turkic people | *A creamy sauce with pickles
exercise: «Grandma needs cream of tartar for the cake.» What is cream of tartar used for? | *Baking | Cooking a fish supper | Brushing teeth | Scraping plaque off teeth
test: «Plaque left for days can harden into tartar.» Where does tartar build up? | In a cake | *On the teeth | On a bus | In the sea
test: «The old teacher was a tartar, always shouting at the class.» What does tartar mean here? | A hard coating on teeth | A creamy sauce | A member of the Tatar people | *A fierce, bad-tempered person
exam: The sentence «Crimean Tatars are a people of Crimea in Ukraine» shows that tartar, as Tatar, means | *A group of people | A creamy sauce | A white powder used in baking | A hard coating on teeth
